{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524111-four-homebrew-artifacts-something-more","id":1524111,"title":"Four Homebrew artifacts + something more","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-15T10:58:39-07:00","id":1524111,"title":"Four Homebrew artifacts + something more","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eye of Ajna (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</span><br /> Gnosis: 3 Mind: 4 Mana: 12<br /> <br /> The Eye of Ajna is a Pandemonic artifact that appears as a cloudy, gray, third eye. The eye alters the mage\u2019s other eyes to appear the same. These alterations are not hidden from the eyes of sleepers and cause dissonance and quiescence, therefore, the mage with the Eye of Ajna must find ways to hide the effects or avoid sleepers.<br /> <br /> The artifact has several effects relating in Supurnal, Pandemonic, insights into the vices, aspirations and obsessions of those the Eye of Ajna can see. The first effect is straightforward, the artifact reveals the aspirations and vices of the target. If the target is a mage, their obsessions are also revealed. The mage is able to see these as the goetia that represent them in the mind of the target and has an intuitive sense of what they represent.<br /> <br /> The second effect of the artifact allows the mage to summon the revealed goetia out of the Oniros of someone targeted by the first effect and grant them the materialized condition. This effect lasts for one hour or a scene, whichever comes first, at the end of which the goetia returns to the Oniros it was summoned from.<br /> <br /> All of this leads up to the final effect. A manifested goetia can be targeted by the Eye of Ajna. The artifact or the mage wielding it must spend a point of mana, which creates a connection between the goetia and Pandemonium. Truth from the Supernal realm related to the nature of the goetia infuses the entity, altering it and granting it insights into its nature. Once returned to its Oniros it causes the persistent obsession condition on the person it is a part of, with the fulfillment of the vice, aspiration, or obsession the goetia represents being the fication of the condition. Once the condition is resolved the target understands the new insights from Pandemonium, resolving the condition and causing a breaking point in sleepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Gnosis: 2 Space: 3 Mana: 6<br /> <br /> Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo is an Pandemonic artifact that takes the form of a Nodachi (Size 3, +3 Damage, -3 initiative, Strength 3) with a bright red blade and sheath. If the mage wielding the Nodachi smears their own blood on the blade of the sword (1 lethal damage worth), Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo\u2019s damage can be converted to damage towards the target\u2019s sympathetic links. This ability lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Weak links can take 3 damage before being destroyed, medium links can take 5 damage, strong links can take 7, and connected links can take 9.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hand of Midas (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Gnosis: 2 Matter: 4 Prime: 4 Mana: 8<br /> <br /> The Hand of Midas is a Stygian artifact that looks like a loose flitting orichalcum glove, an empty cup on the top of the hand, and an overflowing cup in the palm. The magic of the artifact is simple but powerful: anything that falls under the preview of the Prime arcana may be patterned into gold. This effect is lasting.<br /> <br /> The Hand of Midas is directly linked to the Chancellor and her servants have had it since it came into the Fallen World four-thousand years ago. The artifact is also the origin of the Disciples of Midas as they shape their souls to conform to its symbolism.<br /> <br /> Banishers have long sought after this artifact in hopes of finding a way to weaponize it against the Pentacle and the Throne alike.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sarcophagus of the Netjeru (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Gnosis: 2 Life: 4 Matter: 4 Mana: 8<br /> <br /> This orichalcum Sarcophagus is a Stygian artifact. The entire piece appears to be made of one slab of gold, with the only seams separating the lid from the rest of it. It is covered in runes in High Speech, symbols of the Chancellor, describing the method that allows for the dirt of the masses of humanity to gain worth, transformation.<br /> <br /> When a living human is placed within the Sarcophagus of the Netjeru for a full day with the lid sealed, they transform, becoming more like the gods, worthy and valuable in their transformation. The artifact Patterns living humans into solid orichalcum to be melted down for wealth or to be used for other, more nefarious purposes. (See Gold Golems)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gold Golems</span><br /> <br /> The Gold Golems were once human but have been transmuted into servants of the Chancellor. When transformed into a statue of gold by the Sarcophagus of the Netjeru a Gold Golem can be made. The process involves carving into the flesh of what was once a human symbol of service and of the Chancellor and needs to be done within the first day after the artifact has transformed the person. While magic cannot be used to create the inscriptions, that must be done by hand, spells like the Matter rote \u201cShaping\u201d can be used to get the statue into a more suitable pose for the work to be done. The orichalcum that make up the statues are hardened beyond the density that the metal or its fallen counterpart usually exhibit, making the Gold Golems good shields for high ranking members of the Mammon Ministry. It also sometimes pays to be able to send the likeness of a loved one after an enemy, now golden and trying to kill you.<br /> <br /> The Gold Golems lose all skill dots upon their transformation by the Sarcophagus of the Netjeru, but the ritual to transform them from statue to servitor hardens the metal they are made of. They have Power 5, Finesse 1, and Resistance 5. They have an armor rating of 2/2. Each one has a circle carved into their forehead, if a mage's shadow name is placed in this circle in the blood of the named mage, the named mage may transfer the control of one spell to the golem. As long as the name remains on the forehead that spell remains, but the mage may also choose to end the spell at any time as if it were still under their control.<br /> <br /> Finally, control over the Gold Golems is in the hands of the highest ranking mage in service to the Chancellor to have used the Sarcophagus of the Netjeru. The servitors will default to the mage whose name is linked to them, but should a higher rank mage give them new orders they will follow those orders. While status within the Ministry of Mammon is a good indicator of who will have control over the Gold Golems it is not necessarily the guarantee, so the mage who can control them over the others tends to be seen as the new leader of the local ministry by decree of the Chancellor. Some supernal entities linked to the Chancellor have been able to control them in the past as well.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-08-2024, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T13:03:07-07:00","id":1524149,"title":"","content":"Overall very interesting Artifacts. I think it would be interesting if there was an example of a goetia modified by the Eye of Ajna, to provide a feel to how the transformation affects it and what kind of lessons it would teach.<br /> <br /> In the case of the <i>Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo</i>, I think the idea was that the design of the sword and sheathe represent cutting the red string of fate, correct ? How many attacks to sympathetic links does one coating of blood provide, or alternatively, how long does this ability stay active ? Lastly, does the effect end if the blood is wiped away ?<br /> <br /> If the Shadow Name on the gold golems is scratched out, does the golem become unable to hold the spell any longer ? Regarding the fact that they are made to serve the Chancellor, do the gold golems obey only the mage who created them ? Would they prioritize the orders of a higher ranked member of the Ministry ? Could a summoned servant of the Chancellor give them orders ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T20:33:28-07:00","id":1524176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524111-four-homebrew-artifacts-something-more?p=1524149#post1524149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall very interesting Artifacts. I think it would be interesting if there was an example of a goetia modified by the Eye of Ajna, to provide a feel to how the transformation affects it and what kind of lessons it would teach.<br /> <br /> In the case of the <i>Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo</i>, I think the idea was that the design of the sword and sheathe represent cutting the red string of fate, correct ? How many attacks to sympathetic links does one coating of blood provide, or alternatively, how long does this ability stay active ? Lastly, does the effect end if the blood is wiped away ?<br /> <br /> If the Shadow Name on the gold golems is scratched out, does the golem become unable to hold the spell any longer ? Regarding the fact that they are made to serve the Chancellor, do the gold golems obey only the mage who created them ? Would they prioritize the orders of a higher ranked member of the Ministry ? Could a summoned servant of the Chancellor give them orders ?</div> </div> </div> </div>good questions! ill edit to clarify things later this week when im not preping for my game. As for goetia, as soon one of my players has this done to them I'll come back here and share it also","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T20:39:18-07:00","id":1524177,"title":"","content":"As for <i>Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo</i> (Don't ask me what that means its been a year since I came up with that name) my brother and I were gonna run a 1-on-1 Brotherhood of the Demon Wind chronicle which never happened, but he wanted to have to go around collecting aretifacts he used in Arcadia during his awakening. This is the only one that survived though, I didn't care for the others when the game ended up not going through \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T21:31:13-07:00","id":1524180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524111-four-homebrew-artifacts-something-more?p=1524177#post1524177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for <i>Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo</i> (Don't ask me what that means its been a year since I came up with that name)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a loosely translated and transliterated &quot;[The] Severed Binding,&quot; spacing out the past-tense passive conjugation of the verb (<i>-sareta</i> being the past-tense of -<i>sareru</i> being the passive form of <i>suru</i>, the basic &quot;to do&quot; verb that you stick on the end of a noun to verb it like is happening here with <i>setsudan</i> being &quot;severance&quot; or &quot;disconnection&quot;) and using a loanword instead of a native Japanese term (<i>baindo</i> being literally the word &quot;bind&quot; rendered into Japanese phonemes). If I had to hazard a guess it'd be written \u5207\u65ad\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30d0\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9 unless one wanted to stylize it further or mess around with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_character\" target=\"_blank\">ruby text</a> to add another reading or pronunciation to the name.<br /> <br /> It's apropos for a weapon that cuts sympathetic ties, to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Elaboration on the verb. 10-17-2023, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T16:31:53-07:00","id":1524405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524111-four-homebrew-artifacts-something-more?p=1524149#post1524149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall very interesting Artifacts. I think it would be interesting if there was an example of a goetia modified by the Eye of Ajna, to provide a feel to how the transformation affects it and what kind of lessons it would teach.<br /> <br /> In the case of the <i>Setsudan Sa Reta Baindo</i>, I think the idea was that the design of the sword and sheathe represent cutting the red string of fate, correct ? How many attacks to sympathetic links does one coating of blood provide, or alternatively, how long does this ability stay active ? Lastly, does the effect end if the blood is wiped away ?<br /> <br /> If the Shadow Name on the gold golems is scratched out, does the golem become unable to hold the spell any longer ? Regarding the fact that they are made to serve the Chancellor, do the gold golems obey only the mage who created them ? Would they prioritize the orders of a higher ranked member of the Ministry ? Could a summoned servant of the Chancellor give them orders ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe i've answered your questions here! in the original post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}